{#
    The quote's screens and actions, in one place.

    Expects: `estimate`, and `locked` — true on an Accepted or Rejected quote, which withholds
    Edit / Price and Reject.

    The <nav> itself is `admin/_partials/sales_document_action_bar.html.twig` now, shared with the
    order's and the invoice's. What stays here is everything that is the QUOTE's: the two POSTs that
    mint or settle a document, the Reject control, the link to the order it became, and which state
    withholds each. Those four are exactly what a shared bar cannot know, so they arrive as a
    template path — the `barTemplate` slot — rather than as a branch inside it.

    `pdf: null` below: this <nav> renders only on the DETAIL screen (the quote PDF page hand-rolls
    its own nav, same as the order's document page), and the PDF/Download disclosure's own "Print
    Quote"/"Download Quote" already reach `admin_estimate_quote` — the same route a standalone tab
    here would have. See `admin/order/_tab_nav.html.twig`'s own note; this is the same rule.
#}
{% set quoteFrozen = document_is_locked(estimate) %}
{% include 'admin/_partials/sales_document_action_bar.html.twig' with {
    document: estimate,
    idPrefix: 'quote',
    documentNoun: 'quote',
    ariaLabel: 'Quote detail actions',
    view: {href: path('admin_estimate_detail', {id: estimate.id}), current: true},
    edit: (locked or quoteFrozen) ? null : {href: path('admin_estimate_edit', {id: estimate.id}), label: 'Edit / Price'},
    pdf: null,
    barTemplate: 'admin/estimate/_bar_actions.html.twig',
    barContext: {locked: locked, frozen: quoteFrozen},
    printMenuTemplate: 'admin/estimate/_print_menu.html.twig',
    cloneUrl: path('admin_estimate_clone', {id: estimate.id}),
    lockUrl: path('admin_estimate_lock', {id: estimate.id}),
    unlockUrl: path('admin_estimate_unlock', {id: estimate.id}),
} only %}
{#
    `edit` carries TWO refusals, and the order of them is the route's own. EstimateController::edit()
    asks the explicit lock first and the status rule second, on GET as well as on POST, "so the edit
    SCREEN does not open on a document that cannot be saved" — and its comment names the Unlock
    control on this page as where the refusal sends the reader. So a frozen quote shows no
    Edit / Price tab, the same way an Accepted one already showed none.
#}
